# When to test

Add or update tests when you change behavior, fix a bug, or add a feature users rely on.

Locate existing test patterns and frameworks before writing new tests. Reuse helpers, fixtures, and naming conventions.

Do not add tests for docs-only, comment-only, or formatting-only changes unless the user asks.

Do not skip tests because the change looks small — check risk and existing coverage first.
